{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"7fbafb007a4619a0585535f0d4cd90fd96c0d46d56c8de970a7b1d5a22e735c6","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_8f69ea8aa15948285ce97f8c0e458117b7d7c44be09aaf7c2202cfce7cd08bd6","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound and well-motivated approach to structured pruning of convolutional neural networks. The methodological formulation is mathematically consistent, and the proposed Taylor expansion criterion is effectively validated against an oracle baseline and several heuristic alternatives. The experimental design is comprehensive, covering multiple datasets, network architectures, and pruning objectives, with sufficient detail provided for reproducibility. The work is complete and offers a clear contribution to the field of resource-efficient inference.","paper_id":"SJGCiw5gl","paper_identity_sha256":"c106e0232e6198352e4744e6cd26733bea0e0a67e06904f40d399e861d6097a0","prompt_identity_sha256":"6db9fa39d6e70c02e35d156f7f7dab701d274bb87ba4178f36dd5784c88981f2","raw_response_sha256":"2a0c8881e2906d7c5f087bc5b2e1f11c5874b099666665ec91f8c64317201a7e","request_identity_sha256":"993f7b131e1ceae48349a1472bd4880e6aab681df6c1fb118c88a9b895ca45de","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"81128e0a522c7a0ea5bc5be6279219c53a0b1e5906cfff81529a1e1437a59ef3","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-008","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016"],"review_text":"The proposed method is well-formulated and mathematically consistent. The authors correctly identify the pruning problem as a combinatorial optimization and justify the use of a greedy approach due to the intractability of an exact solution. The derivation of the Taylor expansion criterion is clear, starting from the first-order Taylor polynomial and neglecting the remainder term with a reasonable justification based on the properties of the ReLU activation function. The method is technically sound, with no apparent conceptual or implementation errors in the core algorithm.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The experimental design is comprehensive and effectively validates the claims. The authors evaluate the proposed criterion against an oracle baseline and several heuristic alternatives (weight magnitude, activation, mutual information) using Spearman's rank correlation. The experiments are conducted on multiple datasets (Birds-200, Flowers-102, ImageNet) and network architectures (VGG-16, AlexNet, recurrent 3D-CNN), demonstrating the flexibility and generalizability of the approach. The use of both parameter count and FLOPs as evaluation metrics is appropriate for the stated goal of resource-efficient inference.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient detail for reproducibility. Key hyperparameters such as learning rate, momentum, weight decay, batch size, and the number of fine-tuning updates between pruning iterations are specified for each experiment. The use of the Theano framework is mentioned, and the dataset splits (training and testing) are clearly defined. While the code is not explicitly stated to be available, the level of detail provided in the paper is adequate for a researcher to replicate the work.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-003","SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013"],"review_text":"The paper sufficiently compares the proposed method against relevant prior work and state-of-the-art methods. The authors position their work in relation to existing structured pruning approaches (Anwar et al., 2015), unstructured pruning (Han et al., 2015), and other compression techniques (reduced precision, tensor decomposition). The comparison against heuristic criteria (weight magnitude, activation, mutual information) is thorough and directly relevant to the proposed Taylor expansion criterion. The literature review is appropriate and up-to-date for the time of publication.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The statistical rigor of the paper is adequate for the type of work presented. The use of Spearman's rank correlation to evaluate the criteria against the oracle is a suitable statistical measure for assessing the monotonic relationship between the importance rankings. The authors report the correlation coefficients for each criterion and layer, providing a clear and transparent comparison. While confidence intervals or significance tests are not explicitly reported, the consistency of the results across multiple datasets and architectures supports the robustness of the findings.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"10c9895c446ef6f614f02f67b0351ef9234d1f999c12369c056d7cf4fa00f51f","paper_id":"SJGCiw5gl","paper_ordinal":95,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"2a0c8881e2906d7c5f087bc5b2e1f11c5874b099666665ec91f8c64317201a7e","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"SJGCiw5gl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"6a260638ccabd3bc5cdbc36cdfabedb9e142b8c9b3622224a35b7a5772ddb7a6","request_identity_sha256":"993f7b131e1ceae48349a1472bd4880e6aab681df6c1fb118c88a9b895ca45de","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1067,"prompt_tokens":16484,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17551},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"993f7b131e1ceae48349a1472bd4880e6aab681df6c1fb118c88a9b895ca45de","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}